      "rationale": "Remove the direct c65 requirement. The full supplied-data/video alternatives permit a graphical quadratic fit: plot measured pairs, infer the residual-versus-t² slope, establish g and uncertainties, then formulate the initial-value law. The independent c65 task distinguishing −x² and (−x)² for arbitrary negative inputs is not universally required before this inference. This is a substantive allowed route; neither the e4 nor ce431 requires closure is asserted to confer any deep Math mastery. The actual experiment/source wording mismatch is preserved as a separate source/P issue. Current-Main informed successor: same whole mandatory P, all cases/axes and whole Math alternatives independently reconsidered by this author in worked-cases-and-necessity.author.json. Original rationale/solutions are preserved with original identity; this native rebinding creates no independent approval. BW3.3.5.1(3)/(4) and HE E.1 distinguish actual data acquisition, graphs and initial-condition assumptions; active OR-P still permits supplied data. No source-strengthening companion is silently substituted.",
